  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe rotary wrap roughs a bar with a D-flat across the seam instead of refusing it as an open mesh.\n\n- Cause: the wrap closed its cover ends with a flat wall at the outermost seam column, sized from the widest radius at each station. A D-flat across the seam leaves the seam column jagged, so the wall touched none of its edges and left loose chord ends (\"mesh is open\").\n- New `multiaxis/rotary_seam.rs` finds the real seam edges: edges whose two triangles sit a full lap apart. It hangs a curtain from each one down to the floor radius, on both copies of the lap. On a plain turned bar this rebuilds the old wall exactly, so the Offset rings output is unchanged.\n- Edges held by only one triangle (real holes) get no curtain. An open mesh is now refused by name before the wrap: \"the rotary wrap needs a closed solid, but the mesh is open: N edges bound one facet only\". On main, a hole no level crossed wrapped silently.\n- `rotary_offset.rs` drops the old wall code and is now 390 lines.\n\n## Pins (`crates/motion/tests/rotary_dflat.rs`, all fail on main)\n\n- `a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement`: flat through both ends and flat over the middle only, at 4 angles each. No cut tip lands inside the part, and the flat's channel gets cut.\n- `a_bar_with_a_hole_in_its_skin_is_still_refused_by_name`\n- `a_flat_channel_across_the_seam_is_refused_adaptive_by_name_and_rings_cut_it`: #9's seam law end to end (about 36 s in debug).\n\n## Readings\n\n- **motion:** rotary 10, rotary_offset 9, rotary_adaptive 1, rotary_links 7, multiaxis 7, multiaxis_avoid 5, multiaxis_rough 5, lib 130, rotary_dflat 3.\n- **app:** rotary_verify 9, rotary_fixtures 4, rotary_letter 3, rotary_field_parity 3, golden_cl 23, operations 117, tilt 8.\n- **Heavy lane:** the two ignored rotary_adaptive tests pass in release (144 s).\n- **Clippy:** clean on motion and app.\n\nChangelog: The rotary wrap refuses by name a work with a non-turned feature across its seam, or a hole in its skin, instead of reporting \"the mesh is open\"; D-flats clear of the seam wrap as before\n\nRefs #54\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nUpdate (51758c4): reshaping the clearing area to the seam ends still left a gouge band at the flat's end stations, so a non-turned feature across the seam is now **refused by name** (rotate the work so it clears the seam). #54 stays open for the real fix: moving the wrap's seam to a turned angle.",
